    "source_commit": "215abfb217dbac7d5f1273282331b9b1866c0479",
    "source_binding": "Fetched upstream source, not the reporter revision. Package constraints and markers are inspected without a dependency installation or runtime import.",
    "finding": "Under the inspected Linux x86_64 branch, the OpenPI lock selects CUDA runtime 12.6.77 and cuDNN 9.5.1.17. Torch 2.7.1 from the selected PyPI distribution requires that exact cuDNN version; JAX CUDA-plugin 0.5.3 permits it through a broader range. Linux aarch64 selects different versions.",
    "vendor_context": "NVIDIA cuDNN 9.5.1 support matrix does not list compute capability 12.0. The inspected 9.7.1 and 9.8.0 matrices do list it in their CUDA12.8 rows. This is a documented-support gap for the inspected x86 stack, not proof that a particular observed crash has that cause.",
    "rejected_action": "Do not upgrade only cuDNN while retaining the incompatible exact Torch dependency. Do not infer installed/loaded library identity from upstream main or jaxlib version alone.",
    "alternate_build": "The official PyTorch index expose a Torch 2.7.1 CUDA 12.8 build, including a Python 3.11 manylinux_2_28 x86_64 wheel. Its separate metadata request returned 403, so no alternate dependency compatibility result is retained. No wheel was downloaded; no replacement environment is recommended or installed.",
    "script_sha256": "55f17e300ab79b6c541f84588e1294e7c3207156fb0531d72f8cbbcc55c065b3",
