  "public_update": {
    "url": "https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi/issues/1065#issuecomment-6108983867",
    "id": 6108983867,
    "author": "manfromnowhere143",
    "created_at_github": "2026-10-11T12:23:54Z",
    "updated_at_github": "2026-10-11T12:43:41Z",
    "body": "@zkailinzhang, one compatibility detail to correct before choosing an environment change: NVIDIA lists the RTX 5090 as compute capability 12.0 (`sm_120`); 10.0 (`sm_100`) is the B200/GB200 family. [NVIDIA's table](https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda/gpus) distinguishes them.\n\nThe 15:00 excerpt reports CUDA out-of-memory through NCCL. The 15:41 excerpt reaches `CUDNN_STATUS_EXECUTION_FAILED`, then reports illegal addresses during module cleanup. Keeping those attempts separate matters: the posted excerpts do not yet establish a particular cuDNN-version defect.\n\nIf this still blocks your training, could you share the following from the failing environment?\n\n- The OpenPI commit and launch command, including batch/FSDP settings and any XLA, NCCL or GPU-memory flags you changed between attempts.\n- The installed JAX, jaxlib, CUDA-plugin, cuDNN and NCCL package versions, plus the NVIDIA driver version and container image digest, if available. Existing package records are sufficient; please omit credentials and private paths.\n- Whether your immediate choice is to repair this environment or move the run to another software stack/device.\n\nI've only inspected the posted logs so far. Those records would let us check compatibility before recommending a reinstall or another full training run.\n\nUpdate after checking the dependency graph: [OpenPI's lock at `215abfb`](https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi/blob/215abfb217dbac7d5f1273282331b9b1866c0479/uv.lock#L1744) selects `nvidia-cudnn-cu12==9.5.1.17` and `nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12==12.6.77` on Linux x86_64. [NVIDIA's 9.5.1 support matrix](https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/cudnn/backend/v9.5.1/reference/support-matrix.html) does not list compute capability 12.0; [9.7.1's matrix](https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/cudnn/backend/v9.7.1/reference/support-matrix.html) does, with CUDA 12.8.\n\nThere is also a dependency constraint: the pinned `torch==2.7.1` requires cuDNN 9.5.1.17 on this platform. Upgrading cuDNN alone would violate that requirement. If your environment follows this lock, we should resolve the JAX/PyTorch/CUDA stack together. This is a source-level compatibility lead; it does not establish which libraries your failed process loaded or demonstrate a repair.",
    "body_sha256": "be9b71e00b7a2fe259c7aab2b906e0f2128b617e42ea5da52b4518a61f91b9bd",
    "verification": "Exact author, id and complete body read back after PATCH. Original comment retained as prefix; appended a conditional source finding.",
